## bpx-council — second opinions

This project has [bpx-council](https://github.com/gabelul/bpx-council) available: a CLI that gets a second opinion from a different model, or a council of them arguing, before you commit to a direction.

Reach for it before an architecture decision you'd have to unwind later, when you've been circling the same bug for a while, or before declaring a task done.

```bash
# One strong second opinion. Seconds.
bpx-council "Is this auth flow sane?"

# Pipe in the real thing rather than your summary of it
git diff HEAD~3 | bpx-council --question "Review this for correctness"

# Three models, three stances, synthesized verdict. Minutes.
bpx-council --mode council "Monolith or microservices?"
```

It's an advisor, not an authority. If your own evidence contradicts the verdict, trust your evidence and say so.

Install: `npm install -g @booplex/bpx-council`
<!-- bpx-council:end -->
